Rem ==================================================================
Rem seedgeo.shoddy — reckoner seed: geo.shoddy, at a keyboard
Rem
Rem Nineteen words: GEODIST, GEOBEARING, GEODEST, GEOMID, GEOROUTELEN,
Rem GEOCROSSTRACK, GEOBOUNDS, GEOAREA, GEOSIMPLIFY, GEODMS, GEOPARSE,
Rem GEOHASH, GEOLOCATOR, GEOCOMPASS, GEOJULIAN, GEOSUNRISE, GEOSUNSET,
Rem GEODAYLENGTH, GEOHORIZON.
Rem
Rem A POINT AT A PROMPT IS A TWO-ELEMENT LIST, { 53.72 -1.86 }, latitude
Rem first, and a route is a LIST of them. A record does not fit a Cell,
Rem and a resource binding would be absurd for a value with no lifetime
Rem — so this is the shape seed-matrix and seed-stats already use for a
Rem structured argument, and it is the one a person can type.
Rem
Rem THE WORDS ARE GEO-PREFIXED, all of them. Bare DISTANCE, AREA and
Rem BEARING are exactly the names the next domain seed will want too,
Rem and a name registered twice does not collide — it SILENTLY REPLACES
Rem the first, which is a fault nothing in the engine will report.
Rem
Rem NOTHING HERE ABORTS. Every guard geo performs with Error is asked
Rem first and answered as a refusal: an out-of-domain coordinate, an
Rem empty route where a route is needed, a polygon of two points, a
Rem geohash length below one. The line is the transaction, and a refused
Rem line must leave the stack exactly as it was.
Rem
Rem EVERY GUARD BELOW TESTS ITS REASON WITH If/Then/Else AND NEVER Ifte.
Rem Ifte is an ordinary call, so both arms are evaluated before it
Rem chooses between them — handing it an aborting geo word as one arm
Rem would run exactly the abort the guard was written to prevent.
Rem
Rem AN Option BRIDGES AS A ONE-CELL LIST: { } for None, { x } for Some.
Rem GEOSUNRISE inside a polar day answers { }, which is the honest stack
Rem spelling of "it does not". LENGTH asks whether there was one. This
Rem is the encoding seed-bool's LOWBIT uses and for the same reason: a
Rem word pushing a variable number of cells would break UNDO's
Rem accounting, so the answer is always exactly one cell.
Rem
Rem GEOJULIAN IS NOT IN THE ENHANCEMENT'S LIST OF EIGHTEEN and is here
Rem anyway, because without it the three sun words cannot be reached
Rem from a keyboard at all: they take a Julian date and there would be
Rem no way to make one. geo takes the date as an argument on purpose —
Rem that is what keeps it out of the capability system — so the bridge
Rem has to come with it.
Rem
Rem STILL NOT BRIDGED, and these are boundaries rather than a to-do
Rem list: the intersection and along-track family, resample, waypoints,
Rem centroid, the box words other than GEOBOUNDS, the geohash and
Rem locator readers, twilight, solar position, and the rhumb family.
Rem They want either two structured arguments and a fraction, or a
Rem record answer with no stack spelling, and three list arguments at a
Rem prompt is where a bridge stops helping.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "geo.shoddy"
Include "cuttle.shoddy"
Include "reckoner.shoddy"

Rem ---- reading a point off the stack ------------------------------------

Rem A Cell holding { lat lon } as a GeoPt, or a refusal naming the word
Rem the person actually typed.
Def GsPt(word As String, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case RckListArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(xs)
            GsPtOf(word, xs)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def GsPtOf(word As String, xs As List Of Cell) As Result
    If Length(xs) <> 2 Then
        Err(word & " needs a point as a LIST of a latitude and a longitude, got " & Str(Length(xs)) & " items", 0)
    Else
        GsPtAt(word, Nth(xs, 1), Nth(xs, 2))

Def GsPtAt(word As String, a As Cell, b As Cell) As Result
    Select Case RckNumArg(word, a)
        Case Ok(lat)
            GsPtLon(word, lat, b)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def GsPtLon(word As String, lat As Number, b As Cell) As Result
    Select Case RckNumArg(word, b)
        Case Ok(lon)
            GsChecked(word, GeoTryAt(lat, lon))
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Rem GeoTryAt is the TOTAL twin of GeoAt and is what makes this seed
Rem possible: the domain check comes back as a value, so the guard is
Rem asked rather than reached.
Def GsChecked(word As String, r As Result) As Result
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(p)
            Ok(p)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(word & ": " & w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Rem ---- reading a route off the stack ------------------------------------

Def GsPts(word As String, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case RckListArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(xs)
            GsPtsAt(word, xs, { })
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def GsPtsAt(word As String, xs As List Of Cell, acc As List Of GeoPt) As Result
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        Ok(Reverse(acc))
    Else
        GsPtsNext(word, xs, acc, GsPt(word, First(xs)))

Def GsPtsNext(word As String, xs As List Of Cell, acc As List Of GeoPt, r As Result) As Result
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(p)
            GsPtsAt(word, Rest(xs), Prepend(p, acc))
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Rem ---- writing answers back ---------------------------------------------

Def GsPtCell(p As GeoPt) As Cell
    CutList({ CutNum(GeoLat(p)), CutNum(GeoLon(p)) })

Def GsPtsCell(pts As List Of GeoPt) As Cell
    CutList(Map(pts, GsPtCell))

Rem One cell holding a list that is empty for None and holds the number
Rem for Some. LENGTH is how the keyboard asks which it was.
Def GsOptCell(o As Option) As Cell
    Select Case o
        Case Some(x)
            CutList({ CutNum(x) })
        Case Else
            CutList({ })

Rem ---- the shapes the words share ---------------------------------------

Def GsTwoNum(word As String, vs As List Of Cell, f As [ GeoPt GeoPt -- Number ]) As RckWork
    Select Case GsPt(word, First(vs))
        Case Ok(a)
            GsTwoNumB(word, a, Nth(vs, 2), f)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Def GsTwoNumB(word As String, a As GeoPt, c As Cell, f As [ GeoPt GeoPt -- Number ]) As RckWork
    Select Case GsPt(word, c)
        Case Ok(b)
            RckVals({ CutNum(Call(f, a, b)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Def GsPtNum(word As String, vs As List Of Cell, f As [ GeoPt Number -- Number ]) As RckWork
    Select Case GsPt(word, First(vs))
        Case Ok(p)
            GsPtNumB(word, p, Nth(vs, 2), f)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Def GsPtNumB(word As String, p As GeoPt, c As Cell, f As [ GeoPt Number -- Number ]) As RckWork
    Select Case RckNumArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(x)
            RckVals({ CutNum(Call(f, p, x)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Def GsPtOpt(word As String, vs As List Of Cell, f As [ GeoPt Number -- Option ]) As RckWork
    Select Case GsPt(word, First(vs))
        Case Ok(p)
            GsPtOptB(word, p, Nth(vs, 2), f)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Def GsPtOptB(word As String, p As GeoPt, c As Cell, f As [ GeoPt Number -- Option ]) As RckWork
    Select Case RckNumArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(x)
            RckVals({ GsOptCell(Call(f, p, x)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Rem ---- GEODIST, GEOBEARING ----------------------------------------------

Def GsSeedDist(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "GEODIST", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => GsTwoNum("GEODIST", vs, GeoDistance)), "( a b -- m )", "The great-circle distance in metres between two points, each a LIST of a latitude and a longitude in degrees.")

Def GsSeedBearing(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "GEOBEARING", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => GsTwoNum("GEOBEARING", vs, GeoBearing)), "( a b -- deg )", "The initial bearing from a to b, degrees clockwise from north. It changes along the way; this is the one you leave on.")

Rem ---- GEODEST ----------------------------------------------------------

Def GsSeedDest(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "GEODEST", 3, RckPure(Fn(vs) => GsDest(vs)), "( a brg m -- b )", "Where you arrive steering brg degrees from a for m metres, as a LIST of a latitude and a longitude.")

Def GsDest(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case GsPt("GEODEST", First(vs))
        Case Ok(a)
            GsDestBrg(a, Nth(vs, 2), Nth(vs, 3))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEODEST did not answer")

Def GsDestBrg(a As GeoPt, b As Cell, c As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckNumArg("GEODEST", b)
        Case Ok(brg)
            GsDestAt(a, brg, c)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEODEST did not answer")

Def GsDestAt(a As GeoPt, brg As Number, c As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckNumArg("GEODEST", c)
        Case Ok(m)
            RckVals({ GsPtCell(GeoDestination(a, brg, m)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEODEST did not answer")

Rem ---- GEOMID -----------------------------------------------------------

Def GsSeedMid(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "GEOMID", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => GsMid(vs)), "( a b -- c )", "The great-circle midpoint, which is NOT the average of the two coordinates - across the date line the average is on the far side of the planet.")

Def GsMid(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case GsPt("GEOMID", First(vs))
        Case Ok(a)
            GsMidB(a, Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEOMID did not answer")

Def GsMidB(a As GeoPt, c As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case GsPt("GEOMID", c)
        Case Ok(b)
            RckVals({ GsPtCell(GeoMidpoint(a, b)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEOMID did not answer")

Rem ---- GEOCROSSTRACK ----------------------------------------------------

Def GsSeedCross(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "GEOCROSSTRACK", 3, RckPure(Fn(vs) => GsCross(vs)), "( p a b -- m )", "How far p lies off the great circle through a and b, in metres, SIGNED - positive to the right of the track a to b.")

Def GsCross(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case GsPt("GEOCROSSTRACK", First(vs))
        Case Ok(p)
            GsCrossA(p, Nth(vs, 2), Nth(vs, 3))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEOCROSSTRACK did not answer")

Def GsCrossA(p As GeoPt, b As Cell, c As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case GsPt("GEOCROSSTRACK", b)
        Case Ok(a)
            GsCrossB(p, a, c)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEOCROSSTRACK did not answer")

Def GsCrossB(p As GeoPt, a As GeoPt, c As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case GsPt("GEOCROSSTRACK", c)
        Case Ok(b)
            RckVals({ CutNum(GeoCrossTrack(p, a, b)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEOCROSSTRACK did not answer")

Rem ---- GEOROUTELEN ------------------------------------------------------

Def GsSeedRouteLen(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "GEOROUTELEN", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => GsRouteLen(vs)), "( pts -- m )", "The total length in metres of a route given as a LIST of points. An empty or one-point route is 0, not a refusal.")

Def GsRouteLen(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case GsPts("GEOROUTELEN", First(vs))
        Case Ok(pts)
            RckVals({ CutNum(GeoRouteLength(pts)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEOROUTELEN did not answer")

Rem ---- GEOBOUNDS --------------------------------------------------------

Def GsSeedBounds(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "GEOBOUNDS", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => GsBounds(vs)), "( pts -- box )", "The enclosing box of a LIST of points as { south north west east wraps }. It is antimeridian-aware, so west may be greater than east and the flag says when.")

Def GsBounds(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case GsPts("GEOBOUNDS", First(vs))
        Case Ok(pts)
            GsBoundsAt(pts)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEOBOUNDS did not answer")

Rem GeoRouteBounds aborts on an empty route, so the emptiness is asked
Rem here rather than discovered there.
Def GsBoundsAt(pts As List Of GeoPt) As RckWork
    If IsEmpty(pts) Then
        RckWorkBad("GEOBOUNDS needs at least one point, the LIST is empty")
    Else
        GsBoxCell(GeoRouteBounds(pts))

Def GsBoxCell(b As GeoBox) As RckWork
    RckVals({ CutList({ CutNum(BoxSouth(b)), CutNum(BoxNorth(b)), CutNum(BoxWest(b)), CutNum(BoxEast(b)), CutBool(BoxWraps(b)) }) })

Rem ---- GEOAREA ----------------------------------------------------------

Def GsSeedArea(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "GEOAREA", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => GsArea(vs)), "( pts -- m2 )", "The area in square metres of the spherical polygon through a LIST of points, by spherical excess. The ring closes itself and winding does not matter.")

Def GsArea(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case GsPts("GEOAREA", First(vs))
        Case Ok(pts)
            GsAreaAt(pts)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEOAREA did not answer")

Rem GeoArea aborts below three DISTINCT points, and a ring the caller
Rem closed by repeating its first point has one fewer than it looks.
Def GsAreaAt(pts As List Of GeoPt) As RckWork
    If Length(GeoOpenRing(pts)) < 3 Then
        RckWorkBad("GEOAREA needs at least three distinct points, got " & Str(Length(GeoOpenRing(pts))))
    Else
        RckVals({ CutNum(GeoArea(pts)) })

Rem ---- GEOSIMPLIFY ------------------------------------------------------

Def GsSeedSimplify(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "GEOSIMPLIFY", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => GsSimplify(vs)), "( pts m -- pts )", "Douglas-Peucker: the route with every point closer than m metres to the line it sits on dropped. Both ends are kept and it never grows a route.")

Def GsSimplify(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case GsPts("GEOSIMPLIFY", First(vs))
        Case Ok(pts)
            GsSimplifyAt(pts, Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEOSIMPLIFY did not answer")

Def GsSimplifyAt(pts As List Of GeoPt, c As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckNumArg("GEOSIMPLIFY", c)
        Case Ok(m)
            RckVals({ GsPtsCell(GeoSimplify(pts, m)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEOSIMPLIFY did not answer")

Rem ---- GEODMS, GEOCOMPASS, GEOHORIZON: one number in -------------------

Def GsSeedDms(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "GEODMS", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => GsDms(vs)), "( d n -- s )", "An angle in degrees written as degrees, minutes and seconds, with the seconds to n places.")

Def GsDms(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckNumArg("GEODMS", First(vs))
        Case Ok(d)
            GsDmsAt(d, Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEODMS did not answer")

Def GsDmsAt(d As Number, c As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckWholeArg("GEODMS", c)
        Case Ok(n)
            RckVals({ CutStr(GeoDms(d, n)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEODMS did not answer")

Def GsSeedCompass(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "GEOCOMPASS", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => GsCompass(vs)), "( brg -- s )", "A bearing as one of the sixteen compass points, NNE and the rest. The half-winds are not offered.")

Def GsCompass(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckNumArg("GEOCOMPASS", First(vs))
        Case Ok(brg)
            RckVals({ CutStr(GeoCompass(brg)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEOCOMPASS did not answer")

Def GsSeedHorizon(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "GEOHORIZON", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => GsHorizon(vs)), "( h -- m )", "How far you can see from a height of h metres, in metres. Geometric, with no allowance for refraction.")

Def GsHorizon(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckNumArg("GEOHORIZON", First(vs))
        Case Ok(h)
            RckVals({ CutNum(GeoHorizon(h)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEOHORIZON did not answer")

Rem ---- GEOPARSE ---------------------------------------------------------

Def GsSeedParse(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "GEOPARSE", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => GsParse(vs)), "( s -- p )", "A written coordinate as a point: a decimal pair, or degrees and minutes and seconds, with N S E W before or after and in either order.")

Def GsParse(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("GEOPARSE", First(vs))
        Case Ok(t)
            GsParsed(GeoParse(t))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEOPARSE did not answer")

Def GsParsed(r As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(p)
            RckVals({ GsPtCell(p) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEOPARSE did not answer")

Rem ---- GEOHASH, GEOLOCATOR ----------------------------------------------

Def GsSeedHash(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "GEOHASH", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => GsHash(vs)), "( p n -- s )", "The geohash of a point to n characters. A geohash names a BOX, not a point: six characters is about 1.2 km by 0.6 km.")

Def GsHash(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case GsPt("GEOHASH", First(vs))
        Case Ok(p)
            GsHashAt(p, Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEOHASH did not answer")

Def GsHashAt(p As GeoPt, c As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckWholeArg("GEOHASH", c)
        Case Ok(n)
            GsHashOf(p, n)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEOHASH did not answer")

Def GsHashOf(p As GeoPt, n As Number) As RckWork
    If n < 1 Then
        RckWorkBad("GEOHASH needs a length of at least 1, got " & Str(n))
    Else
        RckVals({ CutStr(GeoHash(p, n)) })

Def GsSeedLocator(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "GEOLOCATOR", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => GsLocator(vs)), "( p n -- s )", "The Maidenhead locator of a point to n characters, IO91wm and the like. n must be 2, 4, 6 or 8.")

Def GsLocator(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case GsPt("GEOLOCATOR", First(vs))
        Case Ok(p)
            GsLocatorAt(p, Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEOLOCATOR did not answer")

Def GsLocatorAt(p As GeoPt, c As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckWholeArg("GEOLOCATOR", c)
        Case Ok(n)
            GsLocatorOf(p, n)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEOLOCATOR did not answer")

Def GsLocatorOf(p As GeoPt, n As Number) As RckWork
    If n < 2 Or n > 8 Or Wrap(n, 2) <> 0 Then
        RckWorkBad("GEOLOCATOR needs a length of 2, 4, 6 or 8, got " & Str(n))
    Else
        RckVals({ CutStr(GeoLocator(p, n)) })

Rem ---- the sun ----------------------------------------------------------

Def GsSeedJulian(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "GEOJULIAN", 3, RckPure(Fn(vs) => GsJulian(vs)), "( y m d -- jd )", "The Julian date at midnight UT on a calendar date. The sun words take one of these, because geo never reads a clock.")

Def GsJulian(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckNumArg("GEOJULIAN", First(vs))
        Case Ok(y)
            GsJulianM(y, Nth(vs, 2), Nth(vs, 3))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEOJULIAN did not answer")

Def GsJulianM(y As Number, b As Cell, c As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckNumArg("GEOJULIAN", b)
        Case Ok(m)
            GsJulianD(y, m, c)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEOJULIAN did not answer")

Def GsJulianD(y As Number, m As Number, c As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckNumArg("GEOJULIAN", c)
        Case Ok(d)
            GsJulianOf(y, m, d)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("GEOJULIAN did not answer")

Def GsJulianOf(y As Number, m As Number, d As Number) As RckWork
    If m < 1 Or m > 12 Or d < 1 Or d > 31 Then
        RckWorkBad("GEOJULIAN needs a month in 1..12 and a day in 1..31, got " & Str(m) & " and " & Str(d))
    Else
        RckVals({ CutNum(GeoJulian(y, m, d)) })

Def GsSeedSunrise(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "GEOSUNRISE", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => GsPtOpt("GEOSUNRISE", vs, GeoSunRise)), "( p jd -- list )", "Sunrise as UTC hours in a one-item LIST, or an empty LIST inside a polar day or night. LENGTH asks whether the sun rose at all.")

Def GsSeedSunset(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "GEOSUNSET", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => GsPtOpt("GEOSUNSET", vs, GeoSunSet)), "( p jd -- list )", "Sunset as UTC hours in a one-item LIST, or an empty LIST where there is none. The same shape as GEOSUNRISE and for the same reason.")

Def GsSeedDayLength(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "GEODAYLENGTH", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => GsPtNum("GEODAYLENGTH", vs, GeoDayLength)), "( p jd -- h )", "The hours of daylight, 0 through 24. Always a number, even where there is no sunrise to have.")

Rem ---- the seed -----------------------------------------------------------

Def RckSeedGeo(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = GsSeedDist(RckSeeding(st, "seed-geo"))
    Let s2 = GsSeedBearing(s1)
    Let s3 = GsSeedDest(s2)
    Let s4 = GsSeedMid(s3)
    Let s5 = GsSeedRouteLen(s4)
    Let s6 = GsSeedCross(s5)
    Let s7 = GsSeedBounds(s6)
    Let s8 = GsSeedArea(s7)
    Let s9 = GsSeedSimplify(s8)
    Let s10 = GsSeedDms(s9)
    Let s11 = GsSeedParse(s10)
    Let s12 = GsSeedHash(s11)
    Let s13 = GsSeedLocator(s12)
    Let s14 = GsSeedCompass(s13)
    Let s15 = GsSeedJulian(s14)
    Let s16 = GsSeedSunrise(s15)
